@startuml review_layout_05_overall
' Review unit 05 of 05 -- see docs/review_layout.md for the series.
' The whole PR: final state against the starting point, git diff 94efaaf 294e031.
' Numbers from runs at 94efaaf and 294e031.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/review_layout_05_overall.puml

title Overall -- the PR from start to end (94efaaf..294e031)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "API" {
  #C8E6C9:GenerateData(..., <b>layout</b>="scattered" | "padded", <b>padded_dim</b>=None)
  one layout for the dataset;
  #C8E6C9:layout="padded" with overlap set -> ValueError;
}

partition "validation" {
  #C8E6C9:compute_min_density(shape, padded_dim), var0's coverage bound
  [4, 8, 8]: 0.03125 scattered, 0.15234 padded;
  #C8E6C9:only var0 is clipped to it;
  #C8E6C9:_choose_split_dim never picks the padded axis;
}

partition "placement" {
  if (layout) then (padded)
    #C8E6C9:var0: generate_padded_indices -> padded_stratum_counts
    -> _first_occupied_per_line, equal weights; no LHS stage
    other variables with the padded axis: _padded_cells per stratum
    a variable without the padded axis: scattered;
  else (scattered, default)
    :LHS + uniform fill, as before;
  endif
  #C8E6C9:ChunkUtils.apportion(..., capacity) restored;
}

partition "report" {
  #C8E6C9:minimum density row: which bound applied, and its value;
}

partition "docs" {
  #C8E6C9:docs/layout_plan.md (plan, measurements, mask declined)
  README: layout and padded_dim; CLAUDE.md: a Layout section,
  the conda-env rule;
}

#FFF9C4:<b>start -> end</b>, case S (density 0.4) vs case P1 (same, padded)
                          start (scattered)     end (padded)
cells per line            1 / 3 / 3.19 / 6      1 / 3 / 3.19 / 8
  (min/median/mean/max along x2, 32 lines)
lines fill first k cells  no                    yes
minimum density           0.03125               0.15234
ds.nc / parquet           14061 / 5396 B        14061 / 5397 B
case P2 var1 (x1, x2)     -                     6 cells, first k cells;

:<b>unchanged</b>: every call without layout writes the same files
(case A, case S byte-identical); serial equals parallel everywhere;

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added by THIS PR |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS PR |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= output that differs from the start |
  | plain | unchanged |

  <b>Found by running the example, and fixed</b>
  * only var0 was padded; now every variable with
    the padded axis is
  * the minimum density clipped every variable; now
    var0 only
  * the bound in force was not reported; now a row
  <b>Open</b>
  * file sizes are equal: the layout changes compressed
    size, and this package writes uncompressed files
  <b>Verified</b>: 578 tests pass.
end legend

@enduml
